Users are represented by [User](/schema/User) and [value](/schema/value). See [users.get](/schema/users.get), [users.Get](/schema/users.Get), [Users.get](/schema/Users.get), and [Users.Get](/schema/Users.Get). Unknown references such as \[Missing], \[users.Missing], \[io.Reader], and \[example.com/pkg.Name] stay literal.

### Examples

  - Read a [User](/schema/User) with [users.get](/schema/users.get). Continue with another sentence.
  - Keep \[Missing] as written.

Numbered steps:

 1. Find a [User](/schema/User).
 2. Call [Users.Get](/schema/Users.Get).

Preformatted text keeps references and indentation:

	[users.get] id: 1
	    [User]

Raw HTML is text: \<script>alert("hello")\</script>. See [the guide](https://example.com/guide?q=one&other=two) or [https://example.com/guide](https://example.com/guide).
